/*****************************************************************************
    jitJRt1 -- F1. A RETURNED SCALAR FROM A NON-RECURSIVE ACTION. 2026-08-05.

    THE BASE CASE OF THE RETURN EMITTER, and the first fixture in this tree that
    asserts through A RETURNED VALUE rather than through a field left behind.
    Every green rung before item 2 asserted a FIELD after the action, because
    `return` called jitDegrade -- so "what did the compiled action HAND BACK" had
    never been asked of any construct.

    ⚠ THE WITNESS IS THE HARNESS'S OWN LINE, NOT A print IN THIS FILE, and that
    is deliberate rather than convenient. jitRunAction and jitRefire print
        === jitRunAction result = N ===
        === jitRefire result = N ===
    from C++ printf, so the returned value reaches the log WITHOUT passing
    through the incant print path -- which matters because a jitted print of a
    bare string literal currently emits the string's LENGTH instead of its text
    (measured, pre-existing, pinned in incant/jitSelfFn's header, degrade count 0
    throughout). A witness that can be silently wrong is not a witness.

    COMPILE ONCE, FIRE TWICE, INPUT CHANGED BETWEEN. 7*3 = 21 and 9*3 = 27 are
    DIFFERENT ANSWERS, not merely different inputs -- the injectivity rule, since
    a pair that happened to agree would prove nothing about when the arithmetic
    happened.

    ⚠ THE INTERPRETED ORACLE RUNS LAST AND MUST. `testing()` routes to
    jitRunAction only `if input.isCoded` (Commands.rtn:663) and an interpreted
    run CONSUMES that -- so an oracle placed above the jitted half silently
    reroutes the measurement to jitRunIfTest and the fixture measures the wrong
    engine at exit 0. Found the expensive way, 2026-08-05.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, exactly ONE stop() (rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;
register(JitLadder);
define
    rtIn;
    rtOut;
    rtF code={
        rtLoc = rtIn * 3;
        return rtLoc;
        };
    ;
rtIn = 7;
print "JRt1 fire 1 setup : rtIn =" rtIn:;
testing(rtF);

rtIn = 9;
print "JRt1 fire 2 setup : rtIn =" rtIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();

rtIn  = 7;
rtOut = 0;
rtOut = rtF();
print "JRt1 interpreted  : rtOut =" rtOut " (the oracle -- want 21)":;
print "JRt1 SENTINEL":;
stop();
